---
title: The poweruser endgame
date: 2026-08-19
---
I often wonder what the endgame for developers and engineers are. I know, even of many of the people who truly are in this field for their love thereof, it's not much beyond a job at the end of the day.

So what about power users? People, like myself, who love optimizing hell out of everything they do? More often than not, those who maintain a dotfiles repo, maybe use Nix, build their own personal library functions, etc...

For me, personally, it's owning our tools. As someone who considers themselves compiler-curious, that means making my own language, and using it to write my own tools. Tailored and crafted for *me*.

I've been playing with the idea of a language frontend for C++ for a while now.

> Ironically, that's how C++ was born!

I envision a front-end for C++ which enforces the newer "style" of programming in the language we've seen become more and more popular since C++11.

- Raw pointers are illegal, or are implicitly shared.

- The array operators use `std::array` under the hood.

- No header files.

  And much more...
